{"action": "shared_understanding_confirmed", "at": "2026-08-30T20:03:31+00:00", "data": {"summary": "Implement the Commerce backend half of managed storefront availability: persist a store-wide status-only, exact, or low-stock-threshold display policy with status-only as the compatibility default; persist per-product allowBackorders with false as the new and legacy default and provide authenticated admin mutation actions; read Inventory's authoritative available quantity through a provider-neutral port using only the store binding's default fulfillment location; return stable structured status, sellable, and policy-permitted displayQuantity facts; and fail closed for non-active setup, provider failure, missing SKU or location, and otherwise untrustworthy stock truth. Align the read boundary to DinkusKit Inventory main 86da623e0a21f174636cd833f8faf932ba219721. Verify the full policy, backorder, setup, provider-failure, and location-scope matrix plus persistent storage compatibility. Exclude visual EmDash UI, live cross-plugin transport, Blocks/template-store rendering, cart/order enforcement, and pool migration."}, "event_id": "0912a2af-1402-4eb5-ace1-e4eb08ff30dc"}
